## Original Content
The film, from 'No Other Land' directors Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor and produced by the Oscar-winning team behind 'The Zone of Interest,' was shot from the rooftops of Tel Aviv and documents Israel's bombing of Gaza.

## Summary
The New York Film Festival has added the North American premiere of the documentary 'NAZA' to its lineup. Directed by Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor ('No Other Land') and produced by the Oscar-winning team behind 'The Zone of Interest,' the film was shot from Tel Aviv rooftops and documents Israel's bombing of Gaza.

## Key Points
- 'NAZA' will have its North American premiere at the New York Film Festival.
- The documentary is directed by Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor, the filmmakers behind 'No Other Land.'
- It is produced by the Oscar-winning production team behind 'The Zone of Interest.'
- The film was shot from the rooftops of Tel Aviv and documents Israel's bombing of Gaza.


